---
import { withBase } from "../../config/site"
---

<section id="acp" class="acp-section scroll-mt-20 border-b border-line">
  <div class="acp-section-content mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-24 sm:py-32">
    <p class="reveal font-mono text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-resolve">under the hood</p>
    <div class="mt-3">
      <h2 class="reveal text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight [--reveal-delay:60ms] sm:text-5xl">
        Simple by design. Flexible by default.
      </h2>
      <p class="reveal mt-5 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft [--reveal-delay:120ms]">
        When a tree composes
        <code class="rounded-md border border-line bg-paper px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[13px] text-ink"
          ><span class="text-agent">&lt;Agent/&gt;</span></code
        >
        with a
        <code class="rounded-md border border-line bg-paper px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[13px] text-ink"
          ><span class="text-ok">&lt;Workspace/&gt;</span></code
        >
        and
        <code class="rounded-md border border-line bg-paper px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[13px] text-ink"
          ><span class="text-signal">&lt;Sandbox/&gt;</span></code
        >
        , the <span class="text-resolve">AML Runtime</span> materializes durable files, acquires the selected execution
        environment, and prompts the <span class="text-agent">Agent provider</span> through
        <a
          href="https://agentclientprotocol.com"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer"
          class="font-medium text-ink underline decoration-resolve decoration-2 underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:text-resolve"
          ><span class="text-resolve">Agent Client Protocol</span></a
        >. A compatible Agent can read files, edit code, and run commands through that Sandbox. AML then collects the
        result, applies the Workspace save policy, and releases resources in reverse order. Text-only Agents can run
        without either resource boundary.
      </p>
      <div class="reveal mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-3 [--reveal-delay:150ms]">
        <a
          href={withBase("docs/concepts/")}
          class="font-mono text-[12px] font-semibold text-resolve underline-offset-4 hover:underline"
        >
          Understand the three boundaries →
        </a>
        <a
          href={withBase("docs/compatibility/")}
          class="font-mono text-[12px] font-semibold text-ink-soft underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink hover:underline"
        >
          Check provider compatibility →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div
      class="acp-map-shell reveal mt-14 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-line p-3 [--reveal-delay:180ms] sm:p-6"
    >
      <svg id="acp-runtime-map" class="block w-full" aria-hidden="true" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet"></svg>
      <ol class="sr-only">
        <li>Your app sends the authored JSX tree to the AML Runtime.</li>
        <li>The AML Runtime selects an Agent provider and acquires a Workspace provider.</li>
        <li>The Agent provider maps its executable into the shared ACP engine.</li>
        <li>The ACP engine starts the Agent process through the Sandbox adapter.</li>
        <li>The Workspace provider attaches files to the Sandbox and reconciles them afterward.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
